GHOST_SDL: Unicode text input (SDL_TEXTINPUT)

GHOST_SDL took a key's text from its SDL key-code, ASCII only (the TODO in processEvent): a
character such as "ż" could not be typed into a text field. SDL reports the text a key types,
as UTF-8 from the keyboard map, in an SDL_TEXTINPUT event that it queues right after the key's
SDL_KEYDOWN. Text input is now started with the system, the key-down event takes the text of
the SDL_TEXTINPUT that follows it (the ASCII conversion stays as the fallback for keys that type
nothing), and text without a key event of its own (an input method) becomes one key press per
character without a key-code.

